[ti:Day 11]

[00:00.00]problem-solving [ˈprɒbləmsɒlvɪŋ]a. 解决问题的
[00:04.56]outfit [ˈaʊtfɪt]n. 全套装备；全套工具；一套衣服； 〈口〉公司；机构 例 All of these tourists are from the same outfit.
[00:14.16]modem [ˈməʊdem]n. 调制解调器
[00:16.68]additional [əˈdɪʃənl]a. 附加的，补充的
[00:20.16]emulator [ˈemjuleɪtə(r)]n. 竞争者；模仿者；仿真器 例 Read the instructions before you use the latest version of the emulator as a big change has been made.
[00:34.68]eventual [ɪˈventʃuəl]a. 最后的，结果的；可能的 例 We'll make the eventual decision after getting your latest item catalogue.
[00:46.44]embody [ɪmˈbɒdi]vt. 使具体化；合并；把…组织起来 例 The company will provide more funding to produce new products that embody Chinese culture.
[00:59.64]facility [fəˈsɪləti]n. [pl.] 设施，设备，辅助物；容易，便 利 例 Some local officials say the fish market should be relocated from its crowded and aging facility.
[01:14.52]handbill [ˈhændbɪl]n. 传单，广告单 例 He was distributing handbills when Amy caught her first glimpse of him.
[01:24.96]precipitate [prɪˈsɪpɪteɪt]vt. 使突然陷入；促使…加速；促 成；引起 [prɪˈsɪpɪtət]a. 突如其来的；急促的 搭 precipitate sb. into action 促使某人行动
[01:36.96]admittance [ədˈmɪtns]n. 允许进入；进入权 例 The journalist managed to get admittance to the manager's offices. 搭 gain admittance to... 获准进入…
[01:50.52]multinational [ˌmʌltiˈnæʃnəl]n. 跨国公司 a. 多国的；跨国公司 的
[01:55.92]intrigue [ɪnˈtriːɡ; ˈɪntriːɡ]n. 阴谋，诡计；谋划 [ɪnˈtriːɡ]vt. 用诡计取得；引起…的兴趣 vi. 耍阴 谋；私通 例 It is uncomfortable to work in a company full of suspicion and intrigue. 搭 intrigue against 耍阴谋陷害
[02:14.28]intrinsic [ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk; ɪnˈtrɪnzɪk]a. 固有的；内在的；本质的
[02:19.68]prune [pruːn]n. 西梅干 vt. 修剪(树枝等)；删减，裁 减；削减(预算等)
[02:24.60]formal [ˈfɔːml]a. 正式的；经过正式手续的，合法的 例 We have no formal collaboration until now. 搭 formal dress 礼服
[02:34.44]aggregate [ˈæɡrɪɡət]n. 合计；聚集；法人团体 a. 合计的； 聚集的 [ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt]vt. 合计；聚集 例 These aggregate statistics concealed in fact the severe income disparities.
[02:49.56]deficiency [dɪˈfɪʃnsi]n. 缺乏，短缺；不足额；亏空量 例 The Chinese government has to deal with some deficiencies in its business environment as infrastructure, education, etc.
[03:06.48]contest [ˈkɒntest]n. 竞争；争夺；争论 [kənˈtest]v. 竞争；比赛；争论 例 Her withdrawal from the contest was a tactical manoeuvre. 搭 contest against 争夺
[03:20.16]mileage [ˈmaɪlɪdʒ]n. 英里数
[03:22.80]quarterly [ˈkwɔːtəli]a. 每季的，季度的 ad. 季度地；按季 n. 季刊
[03:27.84]budget [ˈbʌdʒɪt]n. 预算；预算费 例 The Ministry of Finance consistently overestimated its budget deficits.
[03:38.28]defeat [dɪˈfiːt]vt. 击败，战胜 n. 击败；失败 例 Don't be too upset. Just remember that today's defeat will be the preface to our successor's victory.
[03:52.20]actual [ˈæktʃuəl]a. 事实的，现实的
[03:55.20]proxy [ˈprɒksi]n. 代理人；代理权 搭 act as proxy for sb. 担任某人的代理人 / give one's proxy to sb. 委托某人全权代理
[04:04.32]hazard [ˈhæzəd]n. 危害(物)；危险；冒险 vt. 使遭危 险；冒险做出 例 The rating agency is believed to have allowed a kind of moral hazard to creep into their organisation. 搭 at hazard 在危急之中 / at all hazards 冒着一 切危险地；不管怎么样
[04:24.12]depress [dɪˈpres]vt. 降低；使贬值；使跌价；使萧条 例 The campaign against waste of food will depress food prices in the CPI by 2.5 percentage points.
[04:37.80]critical [ˈkrɪtɪkl]a. 批评的；评判的；紧要的，关键的； 紧缺的 例 Regardless of whether you have taken venture capital or not, capital efficiency and bootstrapping are critical values.
[04:54.84]symposium [sɪmˈpəʊziəm]n. 专题讨论会，座谈会；专题论文 集
[04:59.52]ballpark [ˈbɔːlpɑːk]n. 棒球场；(价格、观点等的)可变通 范围 a. 大致正确的 搭 ballpark figure 大略估计 / in the ballpark 大 致
[05:09.24]proposition [ˌprɒpəˈzɪʃn]n. 提议；提案；见解，主张；〈口〉 事业 vt.〈口〉向…提议 例 This is obviously a paying proposition.
[05:19.80]ill-mannered [ˌɪlˈmænəd]a. 无礼的；态度恶劣的 例 Ill-mannered taxi drivers are hardly unknown in the US.
[05:29.64]insufficient [ˌɪnsəˈfɪʃnt]a. 不足的；不适合的；缺乏能力的 例 We soon realised that we had insufficient money to fund the project. 搭 be insufficient to do sth. 不能胜任某事
[05:45.00]intermediation [ˈɪntəˌmiːdiˈeɪʃn]n. 调停；仲裁；调解；中介 例 This rapid growth in the bank sector did not improve the quality of financial intermediation.
[06:00.00]legitimate [lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət]a. 合法的；合理的，正当的 例 In order to achieve its legitimate purpose, the company must carry forward the project in a certain procedure.
[06:15.60]prevail [prɪˈveɪl]vi. 流行，盛行；取胜；占优势 例 The new rule ensures that only the most senior staff prevail. 搭 prevail against/over 战胜
[06:28.32]wreckage [ˈrekɪdʒ]n. (船只或飞机等的)失事；残骸
[06:32.28]off-the-peg [ˌɒfðəˈpeɡ]a. 现成的；非定制的
[06:36.12]worthiness [ˈwɜːðinəs]n. 价值；值得 例 They have introduced a credit-worthiness assessment and reward system for small businesses.
[06:49.20]semi-skilled [ˌsemiˈskɪld]a. 半熟练的
[06:52.92]pastime [ˈpɑːstaɪm]n. 消遣，娱乐 例 Listening to music or reading is the favourite pastime of many people after work.
[07:04.20]wholesale [ˈhəʊlseɪl]n./v. 批发 a. 批发的；大批的 ad. 以批 发方式；大批地 例 Social change is difficult, and some projects are bound to fall short of what is expected.
[07:19.08]landmark [ˈlændmɑːk]n. 路标；里程碑
[07:22.32]assign [əˈsaɪn]vt. 指派，选派；指定(时间、地点等)；分 配；布置(作业) 例 The business analyst can assign resources and durations reasonably to each of the tasks in the process. 搭 assign sb. a job 把某项工作分派给某人
[07:40.92]analysis [əˈnæləsɪs]n. 分析；分解 例 Statistical analysis is a means of arriving at a fairly reliable forecast. The government claimed that it would improve base pay for professional and technical workers. 搭 in the final analysis 归根结底，总之
[08:04.44]reposition [ˌrɪpəˈzɪʃn]n. 重新配置；保存，贮藏 vt. 改变位置 搭 reposition back to its former state 改变回原 来的状态 specific tariff 从量税
[08:16.08]sustain [səˈsteɪn]vt. 支撑；承担(费用)；维持；承受；蒙 受
[08:20.64]legislation [ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn]n. 立法；法律的制定(或通过)
[08:25.56]venue [ˈvenjuː]n. 集合地点；会议地点；审判地 例 It is not so easy here to find an ideal venue for business meetings.
[08:35.76]notary [ˈnəʊtəri]n. 公证人
[08:38.28]postmark [ˈpəʊstmɑːk]n. 邮戳 vt. 盖邮戳于 搭 commemorative postmark 纪念邮戳
[08:45.12]census [ˈsensəs]n. 人口普查；调查报告 例 He then compared it with the census of 1881. 搭 take a census 调查人口
[08:54.60]meticulous [məˈtɪkjələs]a. 小心翼翼的；细致的；一丝不苟 的 例 He made meticulous preparations so as to display his ability to the interviewers. 搭 careful and meticulous calculation 精打细算 / in a meticulous way 过细地；细致地
[09:15.00]overproduction [ˌəʊvəprəˈdʌkʃn]n. 生产过剩
[09:19.32]ferry [ˈferi]n. 摆渡；渡口；渡船；飞机渡运 vt. 渡运 (人或物) 例 If you want tickets for the ferry, please fill in this booking form. 搭 ferry goods 运送货物 / go by the ferry 乘渡 船去
[09:34.44]know-how [ˈnəʊˌhaʊ]n. 专门技能；实践知识；技术诀窍； 生产经验；技术情报 例 The company has the know-how to solve these problems.
[09:45.24]dotcom [ˌdɒtˈkɒm]n. 网站 例 There are great differences between today and the dotcom bubble of about two decades ago.
[09:56.76]inactive [ɪnˈæktɪv]a. 不活动的；停业的；暂停不用的；交 易甚少的 例 The company was inactive after being struck by the economic crisis.
[10:08.52]notify [ˈnəʊtɪfaɪ]vt. 通知，告知；公布 例 Please notify him that the press conference has been postponed until next Tuesday. 搭 notify sb. of sth. 通知某人某事
[10:23.04]emigrate [ˈemɪɡreɪt]v. 移居他国(或外地) 例 He emigrated from India to Norway to enjoy a better life. 搭 emigrate from...to... 从…移民到…派 emigra t ion n. 移民；移居国外(例：emigration papers 出境证件)
[10:40.92]consent [kənˈsent]n. 同意，赞同；准许 vi. 同意，赞成； 准许 例 Any concessions would have required the consent of all the lenders. 搭 by common consent 经一致同意 / consent to 同意 / with the consent of 经…的同意
[10:59.04]engine [ˈendʒɪn]n. 引擎，发动机；机车，火车头 例 A team leader to a team is like an engine to a car.
[11:07.44]defalcate [ˈdiːfælkeit]vi. 挪用公款；侵吞公款；缺额；亏 空 例 Nobody can defalcate the property of the company by abusing their power.
[11:19.68]advocate [ˈædvəkeɪt]vt. 提倡，主张 [ˈædvəkət]n. 提倡者，拥护者；辩护律师，辩护 人 搭 advocate doing sth. 倡议做某事 / advocate thriftiness 提倡节约 / an advocate of... …的倡 议者或拥护者
[11:34.92]appeal [əˈpiːl]vi. 呼吁；恳求；上诉；求助；有吸引力 vt. 将…上诉 n. 呼吁；恳请；上诉；吸引力 例 That venture company holds little appeal for me. 搭 appeal to sb. for sth. 为某事向某人呼吁 / appeal to sb. 求助某人
[11:51.60]jog [dʒɒɡ]vt. 顶，推；使缓步前进 vi. 慢跑；缓慢而 平稳地进行；颠簸地移动 例 His business just kept jogging along for years.
[12:01.44]index [ˈɪndeks]n. 指数；指标；索引 例 You can see the materials about these companies on the index page.
[12:11.04]haggle [ˈhæɡl]n. 讨价还价；争论 vi. 讨价还价 例 In many countries you have to haggle before you buy anything.
[12:20.76]handset [ˈhændset]n. 手机；电话听筒 例 The margins of handset makers were controlled by the telecom carriers.
[12:31.20]cosmopolitan [ˌkɒzməˈpɒlɪtən]n. 世界主义者 a. 世界性的 例 The downside of being so cosmopolitan is that European jobs may migrate to low-cost countries. 搭 cosmopolitan city 世界性城市 / cosmopolitan culture 世界性的文化
[12:51.60]placard [ˈplækɑːd]n. 布告；标语牌 vt. 张贴(布告)；公布
[12:56.04]entertainment [ˌentəˈteɪnmənt]n. 娱乐；供消遣的东西；招待 例 It's good to have some entertainment after a long time at work. 搭 find entertainment in 以…为乐 / give an entertainment to sb. 招待某人
[13:13.92]demonstrate [ˈdemənstreɪt]vt. 示范；证明；说明；显示 vi. 举 行示威游行(或集会) 例 You need to demonstrate more wisdom to take full advantage of every opportunity and solve the company's problems. 搭 demonstrate against 示威反对 / demonstrate sb's ability 显示某人的能力
[13:38.28]essential [ɪˈsenʃl]a. 必要的；基本的，本质的 n. 本质，基 础；必需品 例 The financial reform is essential to facilitate the future industrial restructuring. 搭 be essential to 对…是必不可少的 / be essential to do sth. 有必要做某事
[13:58.08]deceit [dɪˈsiːt]n. 欺骗；欺骗行为 例 The case was described as a web of greed and deceit that reflected Wall Street's trading scandal existing for a long time.
[14:13.20]query [ˈkwɪəri]v. 询问；(对…)表示疑问 n. 询问；问题
[14:17.28]incumbent [ɪnˈkʌmbənt]n. 在职者；现任者 例 The incumbent should first do something meaningful and then insist on it.
[14:28.44]admiration [ˌædməˈreɪʃn]n. 钦佩；赞赏；引人赞美的人或物 例 With his own wisdom and honesty, he earned the admiration of all his colleagues. 搭 admiration for sb./sth. 赞赏某人或某物
[14:44.76]absolve [əbˈzɒlv]vt. 赦免，宽恕；免除…的责任 例 Mr. Anderson's admirable behaviour in the aftermath of the attacks does not absolve him of responsibility for negligence. 搭 absolve sb. from/of... 免除某人的…责任 excise duty 国内消费税；消费税
[15:06.84]intranet [ˈɪntrənet]n. 企业内部网 例 The people who do not work for your company can't access such information through your intranet.
[15:19.80]conference [ˈkɒnfərəns]n. 同业公会；(正式)会议，讨论会； 讨论，商谈 搭 annual conference 年会 / have a conference with sb. 和某人商议
